WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.439
Spring creates and connects application objects called beans.

00:00:03.589 --> 00:00:08.709
Constructor injection declares required dependencies and supports ordinary unit testing.

00:00:08.859 --> 00:00:13.296
A service should express business behavior without looking up its dependencies from

00:00:13.296 --> 00:00:14.406
a global context.

00:00:14.556 --> 00:00:20.101
Bean scope controls instance lifetime; singleton means one instance per application context,

00:00:20.101 --> 00:00:22.873
not one instance across all deployments.

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:28.634
Several Spring features use proxies that intercept calls, including declarative transactions.

00:00:28.784 --> 00:00:32.759
With the usual proxy-based transaction model, a method calling another method on

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:35.741
the same object does not pass through the proxy.

00:00:35.891 --> 00:00:40.293
This explains why moving a transactional method to a separate injected service

00:00:40.293 --> 00:00:41.393
can change behavior.

00:00:41.543 --> 00:00:47.084
OrderService orchestrates the checkout while OrderTransactions owns short database transactions.

00:00:47.234 --> 00:00:51.716
Calls from OrderService to the injected OrderTransactions bean cross the proxy.

00:00:51.866 --> 00:00:56.960
The HTTP inventory call happens after create returns and before complete begins,

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:00.781
avoiding a database transaction held open during network waiting.

00:01:00.931 --> 00:01:03.095
Draw the bean graph for both services.

00:01:03.245 --> 00:01:06.863
Write a unit test that constructs a pure domain service directly.

00:01:07.013 --> 00:01:12.464
Demonstrate why calling this.transactionalMethod() differs from calling a separate proxied bean.

00:01:12.614 --> 00:01:18.001
Constructor injection reveals the graph and prevents partially initialized required dependencies.

00:01:18.151 --> 00:01:22.722
Verify transaction activity or rollback behavior in the proxy demonstration rather than

00:01:22.722 --> 00:01:25.389
relying on the presence of an annotation.

00:01:25.539 --> 00:01:28.834
Keep infrastructure details out of pure calculations.

00:01:28.985 --> 00:01:29.656
Question.

00:01:29.806 --> 00:01:32.482
Does a singleton bean make its fields thread-safe?

00:01:32.632 --> 00:01:33.209
Answer.

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:33.842
No.

00:01:33.992 --> 00:01:38.639
Concurrent requests may call the same instance, so mutable fields need appropriate

00:01:38.639 --> 00:01:40.575
coordination or should be avoided.

00:01:40.725 --> 00:01:41.397
Question.

00:01:41.547 --> 00:01:45.113
Why can self-invocation bypass a transaction annotation?

00:01:45.263 --> 00:01:45.840
Answer.

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:49.771
The call stays inside the target object and does not pass through

00:01:49.771 --> 00:01:50.716
the transaction proxy.
